---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import FooterCTA from "../components/FooterCTA.astro";
import LandingHero from "../components/LandingHero.astro";
import AboutSlider from "../components/AboutSlider.astro";

// Import assets
import doodleBg from "../assets/images/doodle.png";

// Import slider images
import slide1_1 from "../assets/images/AboutSlider/slide1.1.png";
import slide1_2 from "../assets/images/AboutSlider/slide1.2.png";
import slide1_3 from "../assets/images/AboutSlider/slide1.3.png";
import slide1_4 from "../assets/images/AboutSlider/slide1.4.png";

import slide2_1 from "../assets/images/AboutSlider/slide2.1.png";
import slide2_2 from "../assets/images/AboutSlider/slide2.2.png";
import slide2_3 from "../assets/images/AboutSlider/slide2.3.png";

import slide3_1 from "../assets/images/AboutSlider/slide3.1.png";
import slide3_2 from "../assets/images/AboutSlider/slide3.2.png";
import slide3_3 from "../assets/images/AboutSlider/slide3.3.png";
import slide3_4 from "../assets/images/AboutSlider/slide3.4.png";

const slider1Images = [slide1_1, slide1_2, slide1_3, slide1_4];
const slider2Images = [slide2_1, slide2_2, slide2_3];
const slider3Images = [slide3_1, slide3_2, slide3_3, slide3_4];
---

<MainLayout
  title="About — Sree Kanika Parameshwari Trust"
  description="Learn about the history and mission of Sree Kanika Parameshwari Trust — serving faith and uplifting communities since 2007."
>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <LandingHero />

  <!-- About Us Section -->
  <section class="relative py-24 overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Doodle Pattern: Using inline style and high opacity for guaranteed visibility -->
    <div
      class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none z-0"
      style={`
        background-image: url(${doodleBg.src}); 
        background-repeat: repeat; 
        background-size: 400px; 
        mix-blend-mode: multiply;
      `}
    >
    </div>

    <div class="relative w-full px-10 md:px-20 lg:px-32 z-10 -mt-25">
      <h2
        class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-16 text-[#2C0808]"
        style="font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;"
      >
        About Us
      </h2>

      <div class="space-y-24">
        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <div class="reveal-on-scroll grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-center opacity-0 translate-y-10 transition-all duration-1000 ease-out">
          <div
            class="lg:col-span-7 space-y-6 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#3C1A1A]"
          >
            <p>
              <span
                class="font-bold text-xl inline-block mb-1"
                style="color: #5C1010;">History:</span
              >
              This began as an unregistered trust in March 2007, started in an office
              at Mannarkadu. It was a simple initiative by the couple Ramedas and
              Indira, who decided to renovate their family deity temple, Sri Karupparaya
              Swamy Temple, located on Lakshmana Iyer Street in Negamam, and to construct
              a gopuram there. All family members contributed financially by pooling
              their resources. Under the leadership of Ramedas, construction work
              began in February 2008, and the Kumbabishekam ceremony was successfully
              conducted on 17/03/2008.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="lg:col-span-5">
            <div
              class="slider-container rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-lg border-2 border-white bg-transparent"
            >
              <AboutSlider
                images={slider1Images}
                height="360px"
                interval={4000}
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 2 (Inverted) -->
        <div class="reveal-on-scroll grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-center opacity-0 translate-y-10 transition-all duration-1000 ease-out">
          <div class="lg:col-span-5 order-2 lg:order-1">
            <div
              class="slider-container rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-lg border-2 border-white bg-transparent"
            >
              <AboutSlider
                images={slider2Images}
                height="320px"
                interval={4500}
              />
            </div>
          </div>
          <div
            class="lg:col-span-7 order-1 lg:order-2 space-y-6 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#3C1A1A]"
          >
            <p>
              Following this, even before the trust was formally registered,
              various forms of assistance were provided in 2012 to the
              Jalakandeswarar Temple located on Sundakkamuthur Road in
              Coimbatore. There, 27 Nakshatra trees brought from Panruti were
              planted, and they continue to be maintained by the trust. It is a
              belief in Hindu tradition that worshipping the tree corresponding
              to one’s birth star can help remove doshas (negative planetary
              effects) indicated in the horoscope. Moreover, such practices
              discourage tree cutting, which in turn helps increase rainfall,
              boosts agricultural production, and prevents food shortages in the
              country. Hence, these trees were planted on behalf of the trust.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <div class="reveal-on-scroll grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-center opacity-0 translate-y-10 transition-all duration-1000 ease-out">
          <div
            class="lg:col-span-7 space-y-6 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed text-[#3C1A1A]"
          >
            <p>
              Subsequently, the time arrived again for the Kumbabishekam of the
              Negamam Karupparaya Swamy Temple. The trust members convened in
              July 2019, and after conducting Deva Prasannam (divine
              consultation), it was decided to hold the next Kumbabishekam on
              07/02/2020. With the support of the families who worship the deity
              as their Kuladevam and with contributions from local villagers,
              the ceremony was conducted successfully. On
              07/02/2020—specifically on the auspicious day of Thaipusam—the
              second Kumbabishekam of the Negamam Karupparaya Temple was held.
              The event was organized in collaboration with the general public
              and devotees of the deity, following the Deva Prasannam, under the
              leadership of Mr. Gopalasamy Iyer from Negamam. It was during this
              period that the idea of formally registering the trust took shape
              in the minds of Ramedas and Indira, leading to a firm decision to
              proceed with its official registration.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="lg:col-span-5">
            <div
              class="slider-container rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-lg border-2 border-white bg-transparent"
            >
              <AboutSlider
                images={slider3Images}
                height="380px"
                interval={5000}
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FooterCTA />
</MainLayout>

<script>
  const observerOptions = {
    threshold: 0.1,
    rootMargin: '0px 0px -50px 0px'
  };

  const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    entries.forEach(entry => {
      if (entry.isIntersecting) {
        entry.target.classList.remove('opacity-0', 'translate-y-10');
        entry.target.classList.add('opacity-100', 'translate-y-0');
      } else {
        // Animation for scroll up (re-hide)
        entry.target.classList.add('opacity-0', 'translate-y-10');
        entry.target.classList.remove('opacity-100', 'translate-y-0');
      }
    });
  }, observerOptions);

  document.querySelectorAll('.reveal-on-scroll').forEach(el => observer.observe(el));
</script>

<style>
  .slider-container {
    transition:
      transform 0.4s ease,
      box-shadow 0.4s ease;
  }
  .slider-container:hover {
    transform: translateY(-5px);
    box-shadow: 0 15px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
  }
</style>
